          "text": "The Progressive Alliance joined the SPD Congress in Berlin as @larsklingbeil (our Presidium member) and @baerbelbas were elected co-leaders.\n\nKlingbeil: “The SPD has always been chosen when it had an idea for a better future—when it showed it wanted to shape the future. We need ideas for reforming prosperity, the welfare state, education, and Europe in a social democratic way.”\n\nBas: Social democracy means dignity, security, and empowerment for all—focused on community, women’s leadership, and workers.\n\n600+ delegates advanced a bold, shared agenda for a just, sustainable Germany.\n\nPhotos:\n@spdde Co-Leaders Lars Klingbeil and Bärbel Bas; Congress in session; Lars Klingbeil with PA Global Coordinator @machriscabreros  and the Progressive Alliance international delegation\n\nPhoto: Maurice Weiss/Ostkreuz – SPD Germany"
        },
